# Walk screenshots dropped at the repo root.
#
# MANUAL_TEST annotations cite screenshots by name as evidence ("Screenshot
# c2b-ledger-1280.png") and none of them are committed — zero image files are
# tracked in this repo. They are local proof for whoever ran the walk, not
# artifacts. But Playwright writes them next to the repo root rather than into
# the already-ignored .playwright-mcp/ when a bare filename is passed, so they
# accumulate: 25 of them had piled up by 2026-08-04, ~3MB, from many sessions.
#
# Untracked and un-ignored is the bad combination — one `git add -A` in the
# main working tree commits the lot. Scoped to the ROOT (`/*.png`, not
# `*.png`) so a genuine image asset under docs/ or web-v2/public/ stays
# committable; a deliberate root-level one still lands with `git add -f`.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Compiled binaries at the repo root (an 18.8MB velox-bootstrap Mach-O
# slipped into git via #374 — go build drops artifacts named after the
# package in CWD; bin/ is already ignored, the root wasn't).
/velox
/velox-bootstrap
/velox-cli
/velox-doctor
/velox-bench-seed
/velox-migrate-safety

# k6 writes its run summary next to the script
scripts/bench-rig/summary.json
